WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: uk

00:00:04.891 --> 00:00:11.674
It is very important not to have any illusions - this war will not end quickly.

00:00:11.674 --> 00:00:15.240
Putin said very clearly that "Ukraine does not exist, there is only one Russia";   

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.780
This means he will
try to bring Ukrainians down to the level of an ethnic group, not a nation. 

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.780
And this is an act of
genocide. 

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.780
Europe is prose, Ukraine is poetry. 

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.780
You can live on prose alone, but without poetry it will be
difficult. 

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:33.725
Ukraine, under tragic conditions, is opening new worlds for Europe now.

00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:36.860
This is not the Europe we imagined. … 

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:45.000
We never thought of Europe as a bureaucracy but as a
Europe of values.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.000
 We have never been given any prospects.

00:00:47.056 --> 00:00:52.866
 It seemed that we had left the Russian coast, and the other shore was not visible. 

00:00:52.866 --> 00:00:55.840
Now the opposite is happening. Now the other shore is close.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:03.435
I am convinced, you know, being a Ukrainian, knowing history, being a Ukrainian historian, that Putin has no chance.

00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:05.414
It's only a matter of time and price.

00:01:09.981 --> 00:01:15.371
Tamara Kiptenko: As a historian, could you have imagined that Ukraine would face 

00:01:15.371 --> 00:01:20.370
such a full-scale Russian invasion? Was war inevitable?

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:30.768
It is inconvenient for me to boast, but I have written twice - on the eve of 2020 and 2022 about this. 

00:01:30.768 --> 00:01:38.713
I wrote that the time is similar to 1913 or 1938. I did not say that war was inevitable.  

00:01:38.713 --> 00:01:48.198
But I said that we were very close to war.  In terms of Russia's rhetoric, Russia's behavior, and as the West has behaved. 

00:01:48.198 --> 00:01:58.452
It was obvious that we were going from 32-33 to 39. The question is for how long we will go on this time.

00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:01.101
The question is for how long we will go
on this time.

00:02:01.101 --> 00:02:05.527
Now you can often see a comparison of current events with World War II - how correct is that?

00:02:05.527 --> 00:02:09.400
These comparisons are not entirely correct. It is more correct to compare this war with the First World War. 

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:17.844
Of course, every comparison falters. How is this war similar to World War II?  

00:02:17.844 --> 00:02:29.193
Because this is a conventional war. Much has changed since the World War II, and military technology has
improved. 

00:02:29.193 --> 00:02:36.000
But the combats are still being fought as in World War II, i.e. tanks, planes, bombs.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.567
 I do not see high technology here. And this is the only thing that makes our war similar with the World
War II. 

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:50.255
But unlike it, we dont have big battles. We do not have big fronts. Battles are local, fronts are broken.

00:02:50.255 --> 00:02:57.752
This is a situation reminiscent of the First World War. How else is this war similar to the First World War? 

00:02:57.752 --> 00:03:01.391
Because there is a feeling that the war will end quickly. This feeling was in the First World War. 

00:03:01.391 --> 00:03:06.201
People then believed that the war would be quick and victorious, and we would all return home by Christmas. 

00:03:06.201 --> 00:03:09.133
But they returned four years later and there were 10 million dead. 

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:18.969
The most important thing is the war of attrition. Borders and fronts are stabilizing. 

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:27.778
Sooner or later it will go into trench warfare. Military operations will not play a big role. 

00:03:27.778 --> 00:03:32.080
Stronger rears and bigger reserves will be of most importance. 

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:39.335
That is we should not make any illusions to ourselves. This war will not end quickly. 

00:03:39.335 --> 00:03:41.888
How long, I do not know. But how fast… 

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:48.914
We are not talking about weeks, probably.  It is very important
to switch to the rails of the military economy.

00:03:48.914 --> 00:03:53.284
Tamara: How correct is it to say that this is a genocide of the Ukrainian people?

00:03:53.284 --> 00:03:57.003
Genocide has very different meanings. 

00:03:57.003 --> 00:04:05.137
Lemkin, who was the author of the concept of genocide,
used it in a broader sense than in the UN document. 

00:04:05.137 --> 00:04:15.520
He used the meaning that genocide is an act that leads to the destruction of the people and their culture, including destruction of identity. 

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:23.571
In Lemkin's imagination, the world was like a harp. It is possible to play complex melodies when there are all the strings on it. 

00:04:23.571 --> 00:04:31.034
The disappearance of one string (of one nation) means that the harp becomes imperfect.

00:04:31.034 --> 00:04:40.168
For Lemkin, genocide is not only the physical destruction of Jews, Armenians, and Ukrainians during the
Holodomor, it was also the destruction of their culture.

00:04:40.168 --> 00:04:46.835
 Moreover, this could be destruction by
prohibitions - of language or by deportation, for example. 

00:04:46.835 --> 00:04:54.000
Because in other territories these peoples cannot exist and reproduce like in their homeland.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:05:04.133
 In our case, Putin said very clearly: “Ukraine does not exist, there is only one Russia”. Ukrainians and Russians are one nation. 

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:10.646
This means that he will do everything to reduce Ukrainians to the level of some ethnic group, not a nation. And this is an act of genocide.

00:05:10.646 --> 00:05:13.295
Tamara: What is the purpose in exterminating Ukrainians?

00:05:13.295 --> 00:05:18.943
This is what you should ask Putin. But he no longer thinks in rational terms. 

00:05:18.943 --> 00:05:23.002
Putin talks to God, but this god is the devil. 

00:05:23.002 --> 00:05:28.090
He thinks he is called to a great story - to do something that will save the whole world from the threat of a rotten West. 

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:33.692
Putin is not at war with Ukraine in his imagination. Putin is at war with the West in Ukraine. 

00:05:33.692 --> 00:05:40.671
And on his side is such a pure cool Orthodox Russia, which is called to
save the whole world.

00:05:40.671 --> 00:05:56.567
 It has nothing to do with reality. This means that he will not give up.

00:05:56.567 --> 00:06:03.775
 If there were rational categories, it would be possible to sit down for negotiations. And he says: no, kill them to the end.

00:06:03.775 --> 00:06:06.640
Tamara: Does he sincerely believe that Ukraine was invented by Lenin?

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:14.130
Yes. He believes that Ukraine alone cannot exist.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:19.904
 It does not have the strength to do so, Ukrainians and Russians - one nation, one religion. 

00:06:19.904 --> 00:06:23.149
Therefore, he believes that Ukraine was invented and supported
by enemies. 

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:30.000
It can be the Bolsheviks, Jews, Germans, now - the Washington Regional Committee (Biden).

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:38.960
 A collective West that is constantly fabricating Ukraine for the evil of Russia to bring Russia to her knees every time.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.508
Tamara: Speaking of the whole world, you and your colleagues have repeatedly said 

00:06:42.508 --> 00:06:48.498
that this war will be changeable not only for Ukraine, but also for Europe and the world. First, what s wrong with them now?

00:06:48.498 --> 00:06:51.320
 Secondly, how can Ukraine influence them?

00:06:51.320 --> 00:07:00.000
Timothy Snyder said very briefly that Europe is prose, Ukraine is poetry. 

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.975
You can live on prose alone, but without poetry it will be difficult. Ukraine is opening new worlds for Europe now, 

00:07:06.975 --> 00:07:18.200
unfortunately, under tragic conditions. But we know that the biggest changes are happening in response to tragic challenges.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:24.317
What my colleagues tell me are German politicians from the Green Party: 

00:07:24.317 --> 00:07:35.581
in Germany, taxes on the army have been reduced every year. They believed that war was no longer possible. 

00:07:35.581 --> 00:07:42.385
There is such a general illusion - we have been without a war on the European continent for 80 years, it can never happen again. 

00:07:42.385 --> 00:07:51.247
The best way to ensure peace is to have a strong army. Europe did not do that, it is almost disarmed now.

00:07:51.247 --> 00:08:06.862
Secondly, it must be honestly said that if Russia hates the West, the West is in love with Russia - great Russian culture, great people. 

00:08:06.862 --> 00:08:12.551
We see this in the case of useful idiots, but not only there. In that context, Ukrainians did not look very good. 

00:08:12.551 --> 00:08:20.226
Ukrainians were savages, nationalists, anti-Semites, and so on. And even 2014 did not change that. Only now they begin to open their eyes…

00:08:20.226 --> 00:08:25.982
And third and very important: this is not the Europe we imagined.

00:08:25.982 --> 00:08:32.251
 This is a Europe that cannot make
decisions, because every decision takes a very long time. 

00:08:32.251 --> 00:08:45.613
We never thought of Europe as a bureaucracy but as a Europe of values. Europe, which leads to emancipation, the liberation of people. 

00:08:45.613 --> 00:08:50.526
Why do we like Europe so much? Because Europe is emancipation. 

00:08:50.526 --> 00:08:54.400
She has a lot of problems, of course, she had wars and crises. 

00:08:54.400 --> 00:09:07.128
But almost every crisis ends in emancipation, whether of nations, classes, women, or African- Americans. 

00:09:07.128 --> 00:09:12.240
Relatively speaking, freedom is a symbol of Europe. And this is something that never existed in Russia.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:20.504
Tamara: If we talk about Europe, are they behaving differently now?

00:09:20.504 --> 00:09:29.557
Yes, now they are behaving in a completely new way. Of course, the West deserves criticism and they accept it normally. 

00:09:29.557 --> 00:09:36.610
We would like the West to support us more actively. We deserve it, and this criticism is fair.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:42.366
I want to say that this is not the main thing in my opinion. Two other things are most important to me. 

00:09:42.366 --> 00:09:48.771
First, Ukraine has had many warriors and revolutions over the last 100 years of its history -

00:09:48.771 --> 00:09:55.419
 but it has always been alone; the West was mostly on Russia's side.

00:09:55.419 --> 00:10:01.607
Now, for the first time in our history, we have the geopolitical support of the whole West. 

00:10:01.607 --> 00:10:07.903
And it is not just a matter of separate support for Washington or Brussels, but for Washington and Brussels together. 

00:10:07.903 --> 00:10:09.903
This is very important for us.

00:10:09.903 --> 00:10:18.618
 What Putin was counting on was that the West would silently swallow his aggression against Ukraine just as it had swallowed it against Georgia. 

00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:22.374
He had this feeling,
but it's good that he's so wrong. 

00:10:22.374 --> 00:10:30.481
Putin is a poor strategist. Hopeless. He believed that when this aggression against Ukraine took place, 

00:10:30.481 --> 00:10:38.858
the West would be weak, divided, and this would allow Putin to talk to everyone individually - with France, Italy, America. 

00:10:38.858 --> 00:10:45.100
He did not succeed. The West proved very strong here.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:50.451
Tamara: You said that any war is not only destruction but also an acceleration. 

00:10:50.451 --> 00:10:58.315
But we see that our infrastructure and economy have been destroyed. What will the acceleration in Ukraine look like?

00:10:58.315 --> 00:11:13.353
The main acceleration will be Euro-Atlantic integration. Now we are clearly moving in the direction of the West. 

00:11:13.353 --> 00:11:17.194
But we have never been given a Euro-Atlantic perspective.

00:11:17.194 --> 00:11:21.990
 It seemed that we had left the Russian coast, and the other shore was not visible. 

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:25.027
Now the opposite is happening. Now this shore is close. 

00:11:25.027 --> 00:11:33.606
We have a semi-open door for European integration now. Most likely, it will happen soon enough.

00:11:33.606 --> 00:11:38.099
Tamara: Why do so many Russians support this war, including the educated population?

00:11:38.099 --> 00:11:45.246
 There are various reasons. First of all, Putin has had a TV button for 20 years. 

00:11:45.246 --> 00:11:51.164
The level of intoxication of
 Russian society through the media is huge. 

00:11:51.164 --> 00:12:01.703
As a journalist, you know very well how mass propaganda works. Even the sharpest mind gets used to this narrative.

00:12:01.703 --> 00:12:09.810
But this is a partial explanation. The big explanation is Russian culture. 

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:14.674
Great Russian culture, which makes Russia great, because Russia cannot be small. 

00:12:14.674 --> 00:12:24.583
But this is an illusion: Russia is small. In fact, it's all a big bubble. Russia is large in territory, but not in potential. 

00:12:24.583 --> 00:12:32.447
Russia is great in culture, but not in politics. In terms of politics and potential, Russia is small and terrible. 

00:12:32.447 --> 00:12:39.446
And when this bubble bursts, the impression is that something went wrong: we were told that Russia is great!

00:12:39.446 --> 00:12:50.849
I can collect quotes from Turgenev, Dostoevsky, Brodsky, Belinsky - these are not secondary minds. 

00:12:50.849 --> 00:12:53.592
These are the ones who set the tone. Nobel laureates. 

00:12:53.592 --> 00:13:00.861
The level of anti-Ukrainianness and anti-Polishness there is simply outrageous. 

00:13:00.861 --> 00:13:09.508
Both Poles and Ukrainians are the ones who prevent Russia from being great. Russian culture is a large but toxic culture.

00:13:09.508 --> 00:13:12.200
Tamara: So this is a mentality in a sense?

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:18.730
We can call it a mentality. I'm not saying that Russia should be like that. We know Herzen's and Sakharov's Russia.  

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:23.540
But Solzhenitsyn's Russia is already quite like Putin's. This is very important. 

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:29.622
Solzhenitsyn and Brodsky are two Nobel laureates who think not like Sakharov but like Putin.

00:13:29.622 --> 00:13:31.458
This is a tragedy of great Russian culture.

00:13:31.458 --> 00:13:38.578
Tamara: Another trauma that happens to Ukrainians is that their relatives from Russia simply do not believe them.

00:13:38.578 --> 00:13:47.347
If you are intoxicated, and very strongly, it is difficult to find an antidote. 

00:13:47.347 --> 00:13:58.291
There is a thesis that Putin is to blame. It is as if he came and manipulated the Russian consciousness. 

00:13:58.291 --> 00:14:04.598
No! There are studies that show that the Russians really wanted someone like Putin, and very much so. 

00:14:04.598 --> 00:14:08.895
There is an article by Richard Pipes, the famous historian "What do Russians want?" 

00:14:08.895 --> 00:14:10.895
In this article, on the basis of social polls, he proved 

00:14:10.895 --> 00:14:17.880
that the Russians in the 90's wanted someone with a firm hand who would put things in order and make Russia great again.

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:24.000
 And pay attention - both Russia and Ukraine went through difficult 90s. But they came up with completely different results. 

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:30.634
Ukraine has emerged as a democratic state with changing governments, a state that chooses a European direct. 

00:14:30.634 --> 00:14:33.404
And Russia is a country where the government does not change, 

00:14:33.404 --> 00:14:37.944
where the name of the next president is known for several decades to come, 

00:14:37.944 --> 00:14:44.484
and where they continue to talk about Orthodoxy, autocracy,  and other nonsense. 

00:14:44.484 --> 00:14:48.267
About things that in the modern world look like an anachronism of the 19th century.

00:14:48.267 --> 00:14:51.780
Tamara: Is there a chance for reconciliation of our peoples and under what conditions should it happen?

00:14:51.780 --> 00:15:00.373
 In 1943, the French politician Robert Schuman, who is considered the father of Europe, said that we must put an end to

00:15:00.373 --> 00:15:04.817
 this, we need to reconcile with the Germans. But on one condition - when the war is over and when Hitler is no more. 

00:15:04.817 --> 00:15:12.843
And what happened after the war, the Franco-German armistice began with the Treaty of Steel and Coal.

00:15:12.843 --> 00:15:19.545
The key issue was the control of the territory of Alsace-Lorraine - whether it was German or French. 

00:15:19.545 --> 00:15:28.030
The same was the dispute between the French Germans - whose empire was Charlemagne’s? French or German? 

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:31.610
Was Charles the Great French or German? We have something similar with the Russians now. 

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.191
We see how elegantly the French and Germans came out after the war. 

00:15:34.191 --> 00:15:42.284
They declared that Alsace-Lorraine was a common territory of coal and steel. And the European Union began to work around this. 

00:15:42.284 --> 00:15:47.310
And Charlemagne is neither a Frenchman nor a German, but the father of a great united Europe.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:52.282
I assume that the same formula can be used to build relations between Russia and Ukraine. 

00:15:52.282 --> 00:15:57.066
And to declare Volodymyr the Great the father of Eastern Europe, Eastern part of common Europe. 

00:15:57.066 --> 00:16:00.849
And it is quite possible. But not now. 

00:16:00.849 --> 00:16:06.000
Because in order for Volodymyr the Great to become the father of Greater Europe, 

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:10.145
it is necessary to get rid of Volodymyr the Small, who is now sitting in the Kremlin.

00:16:10.145 --> 00:16:15.955
This is not possible now. But that doesn't mean we shouldn't work and think about this reconciliation. 

00:16:15.955 --> 00:16:20.130
But peace will come at the price of our victory.
 

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:26.913
But I am convinced, you know, being a Ukrainian, knowing history, that Putin has no chance. 

00:16:26.913 --> 00:16:30.669
It's only a matter of time and price which, unfortunately, we will have to pay. 

00:16:30.669 --> 00:16:37.320
It is not our choice, but that's what we will have to do.

